            <ArticleTitle>Lumbar discal cyst as a cause of radiculopathy: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>675-677</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lumbar discal cysts are rare entities causing radicular pain with unknown etiologies. We report a case of a 42-year-old man who developed radiculopathy secondary to a lumbar discal cyst. Our case sheds some light on anatomy, possible etiological association and clinical course which can help management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
